	(text "FB (Feedback): Monitors the output voltage and feeds it back to the internal\n   control loop to keep the output stable at 3.3V\nSW (Switching Node): Outputs high-frequency power pulses (from internal MOSFETs)\n   that feed the inductor to step down the voltage\n-------------------------\nOutput Inductor: Converts the high-frequency voltage pulses coming from the SW\n   pin into a continuous, smooth DC current. It stores energy in its magnetic\n   field during the ON phase and releases it to the load during the OFF phase\n-------------------------\nThe resistor voltage divider scales down the output voltage so that when VOUT\nreaches 3.3V, the voltage at the FB pin equals exactly 0.6V.\n\nNote: C2 must be after L1 but before R15//R16"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 62.23 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.5 0.5)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "37a63538-7e6b-42e6-b08f-446e3a25a524")
	)
	(text "STATUS LEDS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
